## THE OPERATIONAL LESSON (worth more than the patch)

Backing a hunk out of a shared hot file is NOT sufficient to avoid absorption,
and can be actively harmful: while this arm was being careful in one direction,
the sister committed the same file in the other, and the "careful" revert then
became a silent deletion of a landed gate. **Before reverting a hunk out of a
shared file, check whether HEAD already contains it** — `git diff` showing your
lines with a `-` prefix means they are in HEAD, not in your working tree only.

